<section class="program-dossier__panel" id="program-panel-tccp" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="program-tab-tccp">
  <header class="program-dossier__masthead">
    <div><p class="research-eyebrow">TCCP / research orientation</p><h3>Typed context, compiled into human-readable work.</h3></div>
    <p>TCCP studies how a source-bound representation can become an interface, prompt, or teaching artifact without losing the distinctions that make it reviewable.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="program-dossier__layout">
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">Core question</p><strong>What must remain visible when a context moves from source to interaction?</strong><p>Purpose, source identity, claim class, uncertainty, and the next accountable decision belong to the working object—not to an invisible appendix.</p></section>
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">Working grammar</p><dl><div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Material directly inspected at a named boundary.</dd></div><div><dt>Projection</dt><dd>A new surface that keeps a tether to its source and omissions.</dd></div><div><dt>Receipt</dt><dd>An account of an attempt, not proof or release.</dd></div></dl></section>
  </div>
  <section class="program-dossier__sequence" aria-label="TCCP study sequence"><div><span>01</span><strong>Frame</strong><p>Name the inquiry, audience, and no-touch boundary.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Represent</strong><p>Classify the material and map the relations that matter.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Compile</strong><p>Render the smallest fitting prompt, interface, or public artifact.</p></div><div><span>04</span><strong>Return</strong><p>Attach a check, limit, and human-held next decision.</p></div></section>
  <aside class="program-dossier__boundary"><strong>Public boundary</strong><p>This is a public-learning orientation to a research program. It does not expose private research material, claim a production compiler, or establish a standard.</p></aside>
</section>
